<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Burgraviate of Nuremberg</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Burgrave of Nuremberg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Burgraviate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nuremberg">Nuremberg</a> was the office and territory of the burgraves who commanded the imperial castle of Nuremberg for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a>. From about 1192 it was held by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-hohenzollern">Hohenzollerns</a>, who built up lands in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franconia">Franconia</a> around Ansbach and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayreuth">Bayreuth</a>. Burgrave Frederick VI became elector of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> in 1415, and in 1427 the family sold its castle at Nuremberg to the city.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/burgraviate-of-nuremberg.jpg" alt="Burgraviate of Nuremberg" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: --TECHNOKRAT (talk) 14:55, 2 October 2008 (UTC) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Burgraves_of_Nuremberg_(Eigener_Entwurf_Version_2).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
